.TH BZ3DIFF 1 "2026-10-20" "bzip3-rs" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bz3diff, bz3cmp \- compare possibly compressed files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bz3diff
.RI [ diff_options ]
.I file
.RI [ file ]
.br
.B bz3cmp
.RI [ cmp_options ]
.I file
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bz3diff
compares files with
.BR diff ,
and
.B bz3cmp
compares them with
.BR cmp .
Options are passed through to the comparison tool.
A file starting with the
.B BZ3v1
magic is decompressed with
.B "bzip3 \-dcfq"
; any other file is read directly.
.PP
With one file, the plain form of
.I file.bz3
is compared against
.IR file .
With two files, each side is decompressed as needed and fed to the
tool. Two plain files are compared directly.
Missing files report
.I "not found or not a regular file"
and exit 1.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status is that of the comparison tool: 0 for equal files,
1 for differing files, 2 on error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bzip3 (1),
.BR diff (1),
.BR cmp (1),
.BR bz3grep (1),
.BR bz3more (1)
